url: "https://github.com/Nizoka/zipnative-mcp"
abstract: >-
  Model Context Protocol (MCP) server bridging the zero-dependency zipnative
  ZIP engine to AI clients. Provides 15 tools for deterministic, reproducible
  archive creation (store / deflate, a pinned pure-TypeScript encoder for
  identical bytes on every runtime, worker-parallel and streamed writers),
  listing and forensic inspection without extraction (with determinism and
  security assertions for CI), random-access reads of single entries,
  secure-by-default extraction (zip-slip, decompression-bomb, symlink,
  duplicate-path and Windows-device-name refusals with frozen ZIP_* error
  codes), one-call deep integrity verification, forward scanning of truncated
  or unseekable streams, incremental modification without recompression,
  canonicalization of any archive into the reproducible form, merging without
  recompression, byte-range reads of archives larger than memory,
  CRC-32, bounded raw-DEFLATE inflation, an offline capability preflight and
  human-in-the-loop governance issue drafting. Every archive the server writes
  is validated against ISO/IEC 21320-1:2015 by an engine-independent validator
  in continuous integration. Speaks MCP 2026-07-28 with automatic fallback for
  2025-era clients and makes no network call, ever.
license: MIT
